 a runtime case requiring a guard or schema.
3. Explain how {topic} affects a function or module boundary.
4. Write a negative type test with `@ts-expect-error`.
5. Describe a bug caused by confusing static and runtime guarantees.

{refs(category)}
'''

def category_page(category,topics):
    links=[]
    for topic in topics:
        if category=="Start Here" and topic=="Introduction": links.append("- [Introduction](/typescript/intro)")
        elif category=="Start Here" and topic=="Version Baseline": links.append("- [Version Baseline](/typescript/version)")
        elif category=="Start Here" and topic=="Learning Path": links.append("- [Learning Path](/typescript/roadmap)")
        else: links.append(f"- [{topic}](./{slugify(topic)})")
    extra="slug: /typescript/projects/overview\n" if category=="Projects" else ""
    return f'''---
title: {q(category)}
{extra}description: {q("Focused lessons covering "+DESCRIPTIONS[category]+".")}
---

# {category}

This section covers {DESCRIPTIONS[category]}. Every lesson stands alone while fitting the beginner-to-staff progression.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  START["Learn the concept"] --> PRACTICE["Examples and diagnostics"]
  PRACTICE --> PRODUCTION["Production decisions"]
```

## Learning outcomes

- explain runtime and compile-time responsibilities;
- write a correct example without unsafe escape hatches;
- diagnose a representative compiler error;
- identify API, performance, security, and production trade-offs;
- apply the concept in a project or interview.

## Lessons

{chr(10).join(links)}

## Study method

Run the examples under strict checking, intentionally introduce an error, explain the diagnostic, and finish the exercises.

{refs(category)}
'''

if DOCS.exists(): shutil.rmtree(DOCS)
DOCS.mkdir(parents=True)
write(DOCS/"intro.md",CORE_INTRO)
write(DOCS/"version.md",CORE_VERSION)
write(DOCS/"roadmap.md",CORE_ROADMAP)

manifest_entries=[]
for section in CURRICULUM:
    category=section["name"]; topics=section["topics"]; cslug=slugify(category)
    write(DOCS/cslug/"index.md",category_page(category,topics))
    manifest_entries.append({"id":f"typescript/{cslug}/index","path":f"docs/typescript/{cslug}/index.md","title":category,"category":category,"kind":"category"})
    for topic in topics:
        if category=="Start Here" and topic=="Introduction":
            did,path,kind="typescript/intro","docs/typescript/intro.md","core"
        elif category=="Start Here" and topic=="Version Baseline":
            did,path,kind="typescript/version","docs/typescript/version.md","core"
        elif category=="Start Here" and topic=="Learning Path":
            did,path,kind="typescript/roadmap","docs/typescript/roadmap.md","core"
        else:
            tslug=slugify(topic); did=f"typescript/{cslug}/{tslug}"; path=f"docs/typescript/{cslug}/{tslug}.md"; kind="reference" if category=="Reference and Audits" else "lesson"
            write(ROOT/path,lesson(topic,category))
        manifest_entries.append({"id":did,"path":path,"title":topic,"category":category,"kind":kind})

overview={
"01-05-foundations-to-unions.md":["start-here","javascript-foundations-for-typescript","type-system-foundations","primitive-types","literal-types","variables-and-inference","arrays-and-tuples","object-types","functions","union-and-intersection-types"],
"06-10-narrowing-functions-safety-literals.md":["type-narrowing","functions","type-assertions","satisfies-operator","null-and-undefined","error-handling"],
"11-16-generics-and-type-manipulation.md":["generics","keyof-and-indexed-access","typeof-and-value-to-type-patterns","mapped-types","conditional-types","infer-keyword","template-literal-types","utility-types"],
"17-25-classes-compatibility-inference-nullability-functions.md":["classes","type-system-foundations","variance","functions","null-and-undefined","advanced-type-patterns"],
"26-31-modules-tsconfig-monorepos-declarations-libraries-js.md":["modules","declaration-files","libraries-and-type-definitions","tsconfig","strictness-options","project-references","migration-from-javascript"],
"32-39-runtime-validation-errors-async-decorators-jsx-react-node.md":["runtime-validation","error-handling","async-typescript","iterators-and-generators","typescript-with-nodejs","typescript-with-react","typescript-with-vue"],
"40-49-backends-architecture-domain-type-level-compiler-performance-debugging.md":["api-design","database-types","architecture","advanced-type-patterns","type-level-programming","compiler-fundamentals","performance"],
"50-59-testing-linting-build-security-production-migration-patterns-staff.md":["type-testing","testing-typescript-applications","eslint-and-code-quality","security","production-engineering","migration-from-javascript","common-typescript-mistakes","library-authoring"],
}
cat_name={slugify(x["name"]):x["name"] for x in CURRICULUM}
for filename,slugs in overview.items():
    links="\n".join(f"- [{cat_name[s]}](/typescript/{s})" for s in slugs)
    write(DOCS/filename,f"---\ntitle: {q('Focused TypeScript Curriculum Overview')}\n---\n\n# Focused TypeScript Curriculum Overview\n\nThis preserved route now links to focused lessons:\n\n{links}\n")
legacy={"projects.md":("Projects","projects"),"interview-mastery.md":("Interview Mastery","interview-preparation"),"interview-question-bank.md":("Interview Question Bank","interview-preparation"),"mock-interviews.md":("Mock Interviews","interview-preparation")}
for filename,(title,slug) in legacy.items():
    section=next(x for x in CURRICULUM if slugify(x["name"])==slug)
    links="\n".join(f"- [{topic}](/typescript/{slug}/{slugify(topic)})" for topic in section["topics"])
    write(DOCS/filename,f"---\ntitle: {q(title)}\n---\n\n# {title}\n\nThis preserved route links to focused lessons:\n\n{links}\n")
write(DOCS/"reference/api-coverage.md","---\ntitle: API Coverage\n---\n\n# API Coverage\n\nSee [Reference and Audits](/typescript/reference-and-audits).\n")
write(DOCS/"reference/final-completeness-audit.md","---\ntitle: Final Completeness Audit\n---\n\n# Final Completeness Audit\n\nSee [current completeness audit](/typescript/reference-and-audits/final-completeness-audit).\n")

legacy_paths=[f"docs/typescript/{x}" for x in list(overview)+list(legacy)]+["docs/typescript/reference/api-coverage.md","docs/typescript/reference/final-completeness-audit.md"]
manifest={"baselineDate":"2026-08-01","typescriptVersion":"7.0.2","nodeCiVersion":"24","categoryCount":len(CURRICULUM),"topicCount":sum(len(x["topics"]) for x in CURRICULUM),"entries":manifest_entries,"legacyPaths":legacy_paths}
write(ROOT/"scripts/typescript-curriculum-manifest.json",json.dumps(manifest,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+"\n")

sidebar=["/** Focused TypeScript navigation layered over shared sidebars. */","const sidebars = require('./sidebars.javascript.js');","","const category = (label, items, extra = {}) => ({type: 'category', label, items, ...extra});","const doc = (id, label) => ({type: 'doc', id: `typescript/${id}`, label});","","s